<title>UK: UK sets HQ for Cattle Movement Service.</title>
<headline>UK sets HQ for Cattle Movement Service.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain is to set up a computerised national office for tracing the movement of cattle -- a key requirement if the ban on beef exports is to be lifted -- at Workington in North West England.</p>
<p>Junior agriculture minister Jeff Rooker announced the move on Wednesday during a parliamentary debate on the future of the beef industry.</p>
<p>He said it was hoped to get the British Cattle Movement Service, which will employ over 100 people, up and running by next March.</p>
<p>The establishment of such a service was one of five conditions for lifting the EU ban on beef exports agreed at last June's EU summit in Florence.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 5427767</p>
